.TH FPTEST 1
.SH NAME
fptest \- check that floating point arithmetic is right
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fptest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Fptest
does arithmetic whose answers are known and prints each one with what it
should have been and whether it matched.  It is meant for a new port: a
code generator or a linker that encodes floating point wrongly will get
integers and strings right long before it gets these right, so a shell
prompt is not evidence that the real instructions work.
.PP
Each line exercises something a back end has to encode on its own: a
load and a store, an array subscript, the four arithmetic operations,
negation, a comparison, the conversions between an integer and a real in
both directions, and the rounding that
.B int
of a real does.  The rest goes through
.IR math (2)
and so through the library behind it.  The last line is
.B FPTEST-OK
or
.B FPTEST-FAIL
with a count.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/fptest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR math (2)
.SH BUGS
.B exp
and
.B pow
fail on every native kernel in this tree, and have since before there was
a test to say so.  The cause is in the compilers rather than in either of
them: fdlibm scales a result by adding to the exponent field of a local
double through a pointer, and
.IR 5c ,
.I tc
and
.I jc
all keep that local in a register while writing the memory it also has an
address for, so the scaling is lost and the unscaled value is returned.
Two lines reproduce it:
.IP
.EX
double
scale(double a, double b, int k)
{
	double y;

	y = a + b;
	((FPdbleword*)&y)->hi += (k<<20);
	return y;
}
.EE
.PP
Every one of the three emits the add into the return register, then reads
and writes
.B y+4
in memory, then returns the register.  The compilers give the two halves
of
.B y
separate entries in
.B mkvar
because their offsets differ, and neither entry then looks address-taken.
The same code written through a
.B FPdbleword
by value rather than through a pointer compiles correctly, which is the
shape a fix in
.B /libmath/fdlibm
would take; the other fix is in
.B mkvar
itself, marking entries that overlap.
.PP
The test says
.B FPTEST-FAIL
until one of those is done.  That is on purpose.
